  "shortName": null,
  "description": "World Wild Fur Camp is an annual furry camp in Ohio, led by chairman Al CaBone and vice chairman Hund The Hound. The first was held October 5 to 7, 2018, at the YMCA Camp Campbell Gard in Hamilton, with around 50 attendees, and it supports the YMCA. Activities include fishing, archery, a rope course, a climbing wall, zip lining, ghost stories, raves, open mic, campfires, trick-or-treating and a petting zoo, along with a \"guild market\" that works like an artist alley and dealers' den. Attendees are organized into guilds that compete in games.",
